{"title":"38","section":"5704","heading":"Transcript of trial records","lead":"The Secretary may purchase transcripts of the record, including all evidence, of trial of litigated cases.","tree":[],"notes":[{"topic":"editorialNotes","text":"Editorial Notes"},{"topic":"amendments","text":"Amendments1991—Pub. L. 102–40 renumbered section 3304 of this title as this section. Pub. L. 102–83 substituted “Secretary” for “Administrator”."}],"sourceCredit":"(Pub. L. 85–857, Sept. 2, 1958, 72 Stat. 1237, § 3304; renumbered § 5704, Pub. L. 102–40, title IV, § 402(b)(1), May 7, 1991, 105 Stat. 238; Pub. L. 102–83, § 4(b)(1), (2)(E), Aug. 6, 1991, 105 Stat. 404, 405.)","releasePoint":"119-102","ancestors":[{"type":"title","num":"Title 38—","heading":"VETERANS’ BENEFITS","identifier":"/us/usc/t38"},{"type":"part","num":"PART IV—","heading":"GENERAL ADMINISTRATIVE PROVISIONS","identifier":"/us/usc/t38/ptIV"},{"type":"chapter","num":"CHAPTER 57—","heading":"RECORDS AND INVESTIGATIONS","identifier":"/us/usc/t38/ptIV/ch57"},{"type":"subchapter","num":"SUBCHAPTER I—","heading":"RECORDS","identifier":"/us/usc/t38/ptIV/ch57/schI"}]}